  "verbalization": "Glecaprevir is associated with Hepatitis C Virus Infection through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of chronic hepatitis C. The evidence suggests that Glecaprevir is used in combination with other antiviral agents, such as Pibrentasvir, Beclabuvir, and Ledipasvir, to target the hepatitis C virus. These drugs are indicated for chronic hepatitis C, and their use implies a therapeutic relationship with the virus. The high scores in the paths indicate a strong, though indirect, connection between Glecaprevir and Hepatitis C Virus Infection, likely mediated through the use of these other antiviral agents. The recurring mechanism involves the use of antiviral drugs in the treatment of hepatitis C, suggesting that Glecaprevir may be part of a broader class of drugs targeting the virus. The evidence supports the idea that Glecaprevir is repurposed for the treatment of Hepatitis C Virus Infection, aligning with the observed indications for other drugs in the same therapeutic context.",
